"DLMF: §22.4 Periods, Poles, and Zeros ‣ Properties ‣ Chapter 22 Jacobian Elliptic Functions (https://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4)\nciteturn1243view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4\",\"lineno\":125}); Total lines: 189\nL66: Table 22.4.2: Periods and zeros of Jacobian elliptic functions.\nL67: Periods  | $z$-Zeros\nL68: --- | ---\nL69: $0$  | $K$  | $K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$\nL70: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL71: $4K$, $2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{sn}$  | $\\mathrm{cd}$  | $\\mathrm{dc}$  | $\\mathrm{ns}$\nL72: $4K$, $2K+2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{sd}$  | $\\mathrm{cn}$  | $\\mathrm{ds}$  | $\\mathrm{nc}$\nL73: $2K$, $4\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{sc}$  | $\\mathrm{cs}$  | $\\mathrm{dn}$  | $\\mathrm{nd}$\nL74: \nL75: ⓘ\nL76: Symbols:\nL77:     【30†$\\mathrm{cd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【31†$\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【32†$\\mathrm{cs}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【30†$\\mathrm{dc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【33†$\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【34†$\\mathrm{ds}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【31†$\\mathrm{nc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【33†$\\mathrm{nd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【35†$\\mathrm{ns}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【32†$\\mathrm{sc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【34†$\\mathrm{sd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【35†$\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【36†${K}^{\\prime }\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complementary complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【37†$K\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【38†$\\mathrm{i}$: imaginary unit】 and 【39†$z$: complex】\nL78: A&S Ref:\nL79:     Table 16.2 (modified)\nL80: Referenced by:\nL81:     【42†§22.4(i)】\nL82: Permalink:\nL83:     【46†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4.T2】\nL84: See also:\nL85:     Annotations for 【44†§22.4(i)】, 【28†§22.4】 and 【12†Ch.22】\nL86: Figure 【47†22.4.1】 illustrates the locations in the $z$-plane of the poles and zeros of the three principal Jacobian functions in the rectangle with vertices $0$, $2K$, $2K+2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$, $2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$. The other poles and zeros are at the congruent points.\nL87:  |  |\nL88: (a) $\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$  | (b) $\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$  | (c) $\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$\nL89: Figure 22.4.1: $z$-plane. Poles $\\mathbf{\\times }\\mathbf{\\times }\\mathbf{\\times }$ and zeros $\\mathbf{\\circ }\\mathbf{\\circ }\\mathbf{\\circ }$ of the principal Jacobian elliptic functions. 【48†Magnify】\nL90: \nL91: ⓘ\nL92: Symbols:\nL93:     【31†$\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【33†$\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【35†$\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【39†$z$: complex】 and 【49†$k$: modulus】\nL94: Referenced by:\nL95:     【50†§22.4(i)】\nL96: Permalink:\nL97:     【51†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4.F1】\nL98: Encodings:\nL99:     【52†pdf】, 【53†pdf】, 【54†pdf】, 【55†png】, 【56†png】, 【57†png】\nL100: See also:\nL101:     Annotations for 【44†§22.4(i)】, 【28†§22.4】 and 【12†Ch.22】\nL102: For the distribution of the $k$-zeros of the Jacobian elliptic functions see Walker (【58†2009】).\nL103: ## §22.4(ii) Graphical Interpretation via Glaisher’s Notation\nL104: \nL105: ⓘ\nL106: \nL107: Keywords:\nL108:     【59†Glaisher’s notation】, 【16†Jacobian elliptic functions】, 【60†fundamental unit cell】, 【61†graphical interpretation via Glaisher’s notation】, 【62†lattice】\nL109: Notes:\nL110:     See Walker (【24†1996】, pp. 126–131), Whittaker and Watson (【25†1927】, pp. 498–505).\nL111: Permalink:\nL112:     【63†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4.ii】\nL113: See also:\nL114:     Annotations for 【28†§22.4】 and 【12†Ch.22】\nL115: Figure 【64†22.4.2】 depicts the fundamental unit cell in the $z$-plane, with vertices $\\text{s}=0$, $\\text{c}=K$, $\\text{d}=K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$, $\\text{n}=\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$. The set of points $z=mK+n\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$, $m,n\\in \\mathbb{Z}$, comprise the lattice for the 12 Jacobian functions; all other lattice unit cells are generated by translation of the fundamental unit cell by $mK+n\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$, where again $m,n\\in \\mathbb{Z}$.\nL116: Figure 22.4.2: $z$-plane. Fundamental unit cell. 【65†Magnify】\nL117: \nL118: ⓘ\nL119: \nL120: Symbols:\nL121:     【39†$z$: complex】\nL122: Referenced by:\nL123:     【66†§22.4(ii)】, 【67†§22.4(ii)】\nL124: Permalink:\nL125:     【68†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4.F2】\nL126: Encodings:\nL127:     【69†pdf】, 【70†png】\nL128: See also:\nL129:     Annotations for 【71†§22.4(ii)】, 【28†§22.4】 and 【12†Ch.22】\nL130: Using the p,q notation of (【72†22.2.10】), Figure 【64†22.4.2】 serves as a mnemonic for the poles, zeros, periods, and half-periods of the 12 Jacobian elliptic functions as follows. Let p,q be any two distinct letters from the set s,c,d,n which appear in counterclockwise orientation at the corners of all lattice unit cells. Then: (a) In any lattice unit cell $\\mathrm{p}\\mathrm{q}(z,k)$ has a simple zero at $z=\\text{p}$ and a simple pole at $z=\\text{q}$.\nL131: (b) The difference between p and the nearest q is a half-period of $\\mathrm{p}\\mathrm{q}(z,k)$. This half-period will be plus or minus a member of the triple $K,\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime },K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$; the other two members of this triple are quarter periods of $\\mathrm{p}\\mathrm{q}(z,k)$.\nL132: ## §22.4(iii) Translation by Half or Quarter Periods\nL133: \nL134: ⓘ\nL135: \nL136: Keywords:\nL137:     【16†Jacobian elliptic functions】, 【73†translation of variable】\nL138: Notes:\nL139:     See Lawden (【23†1989】, pp. 26–30), Whittaker and Watson (【25†1927】, pp. 498–505).\nL140: Referenced by:\nL141:     【74†§23.6(ii)】\nL142: Permalink:\nL143:     【75†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4.iii】\nL144: See also:\nL145:     Annotations for 【28†§22.4】 and 【12†Ch.22】\nL146: \nL147: See Table 【76†22.4.3】.\nL148: \nL149: For example, $\\mathrm{sn}(z+K,k)=\\mathrm{cd}(z,k)$. (The modulus $k$ is suppressed throughout the table.)\nL150: Table 22.4.3: Half- or quarter-period shifts of variable for the Jacobian elliptic functions.\nL151:  | $u$\nL152: --- | ---\nL153:  | $z+K$  | $z+K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $z+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $z+2K$  | $z+2K+2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $z+2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$\nL154: --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL155: $\\mathrm{sn}u$  | $\\mathrm{cd}z$  | ${k}^{-1}\\mathrm{dc}z$  | ${k}^{-1}\\mathrm{ns}z$  | $-\\mathrm{sn}z$  | $-\\mathrm{sn}z$  | $\\mathrm{sn}z$\nL156: $\\mathrm{cn}u$  | $-{k}^{\\prime }\\mathrm{sd}z$  | $-\\mathrm{i}{k}^{\\prime }{k}^{-1}\\mathrm{nc}z$  | $-\\mathrm{i}{k}^{-1}\\mathrm{ds}z$  | $-\\mathrm{cn}z$  | $\\mathrm{cn}z$  | $-\\mathrm{cn}z$\nL157: $\\mathrm{dn}u$  | ${k}^{\\prime }\\mathrm{nd}z$  | $\\mathrm{i}{k}^{\\prime }\\mathrm{sc}z$  | $-\\mathrm{i}\\mathrm{cs}z$  | $\\mathrm{dn}z$  | $-\\mathrm{dn}z$  | $-\\mathrm{dn}z$\nL158: $\\mathrm{cd}u$  | $-\\mathrm{sn}z$  | $-{k}^{-1}\\mathrm{ns}z$  | ${k}^{-1}\\mathrm{dc}z$  | $-\\mathrm{cd}z$  | $-\\mathrm{cd}z$  | $\\mathrm{cd}z$\nL159: $\\mathrm{sd}u$  | $k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1}\\mathrm{cn}z$  | $-\\mathrm{i}{(k{k}^{\\prime })}^{-1}\\mathrm{ds}z$  | $\\mathrm{i}{k}^{-1}\\mathrm{nc}z$  | $-\\mathrm{sd}z$  | $\\mathrm{sd}z$  | $-\\mathrm{sd}z$\nL160: $\\mathrm{nd}u$  | $k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1}\\mathrm{dn}z$  | $-\\mathrm{i}k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1}\\mathrm{cs}z$  | $\\mathrm{i}\\mathrm{sc}z$  | $\\mathrm{nd}z$  | $-\\mathrm{nd}z$  | $-\\mathrm{nd}z$\nL161: $\\mathrm{dc}u$  | $-\\mathrm{ns}z$  | $-k\\mathrm{sn}z$  | $k\\mathrm{cd}z$  | $-\\mathrm{dc}z$  | $-\\mathrm{dc}z$  | $\\mathrm{dc}z$\nL162: $\\mathrm{nc}u$  | $-k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1}\\mathrm{ds}z$  | $\\mathrm{i}kk_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1}\\mathrm{cn}z$  | $\\mathrm{i}k\\mathrm{sd}z$  | $-\\mathrm{nc}z$  | $\\mathrm{nc}z$  | $-\\mathrm{nc}z$\nL163: $\\mathrm{sc}u$  | $-k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1}\\mathrm{cs}z$  | $\\mathrm{i}k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1}\\mathrm{dn}z$  | $\\mathrm{i}\\mathrm{nd}z$  | $\\mathrm{sc}z$  | $-\\mathrm{sc}z$  | $-\\mathrm{sc}z$\nL164: $\\mathrm{ns}u$  | $\\mathrm{dc}z$  | $k\\mathrm{cd}z$  | $k\\mathrm{sn}z$  | $-\\mathrm{ns}z$  | $-\\mathrm{ns}z$  | $\\mathrm{ns}z$\nL165: $\\mathrm{ds}u$  | ${k}^{\\prime }\\mathrm{nc}z$  | $\\mathrm{i}k{k}^{\\prime }\\mathrm{sd}z$  | $-\\mathrm{i}k\\mathrm{cn}z$  | $-\\mathrm{ds}z$  | $\\mathrm{ds}z$  | $-\\mathrm{ds}z$\nL166: $\\mathrm{cs}u$  | $-{k}^{\\prime }\\mathrm{sc}z$  | $-\\mathrm{i}{k}^{\\prime }\\mathrm{nd}z$  | $-\\mathrm{i}\\mathrm{dn}z$  | $\\mathrm{cs}z$  | $-\\mathrm{cs}z$  | $-\\mathrm{cs}z$\nL167: ⓘ\nL168: Symbols:\nL169:     【30†$\\mathrm{cd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【31†$\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【32†$\\mathrm{cs}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【30†$\\mathrm{dc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【33†$\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【34†$\\mathrm{ds}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【31†$\\mathrm{nc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【33†$\\mathrm{nd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【35†$\\mathrm{ns}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【32†$\\mathrm{sc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【34†$\\mathrm{sd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【35†$\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【36†${K}^{\\prime }\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complementary complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【37†$K\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【38†$\\mathrm{i}$: imaginary unit】, 【39†$z$: complex】, 【49†$k$: modulus】 and 【77†${k}^{\\prime }$: complementary modulus】\nL170: A&S Ref:\nL171:     Table 16.8\nL172: Referenced by:\nL173:     【78†§22.12】, 【79†§22.4(iii)】, 【80†§23.6(ii)】, 【81†Erratum (V1.0.7) for Table 22.4.3】, 【82†Erratum (V1.0.7) for Table 22.4.3】\nL174: Permalink:\nL175:     【83†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.4.T3】\nL176: Errata (effective with 1.0.7):\nL177:     Originally a minus sign was missing in the entries for $\\mathrm{cd}u$ and $\\mathrm{dc}u$ in the second column (headed $z+K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$). The correct entries are $-{k}^{-1}\\mathrm{ns}z$ and $-k\\mathrm{sn}z$.\nL178: Reported 2014-02-28 by Svante Janson\nL179: \nL180: See also:\nL181:     Annotations for 【84†§22.4(iii)】, 【28†§22.4】 and 【12†Ch.22】\nL182: \nL183: 【9†22.3 Graphics】【10†22.5 Special Values】\nL184: \nL185: 【85†© 2010–2026 NIST】 / 【86†Disclaimer】 / 【87†Feedback】; Version 1.2.8; Release date 2026-09-15.\nL186: \nL187: 【88†NIST†www.nist.gov】\nL188: 【89†Site Privacy†www.nist.gov】 【90†Accessibility†www.nist.gov】 【91†Privacy Program†www.nist.gov】 【92†Copyrights†www.nist.gov】 【93†Vulnerability Disclosure†www.commerce.gov】 【94†No Fear Act Policy†www.nist.gov】 【95†FOIA†www.nist.gov】 【96†Environmental Policy†www.nist.gov】 【97†Scientific Integrity†www.nist.gov】 【98†Information Quality Standards†www.nist.gov】 【99†Commerce.gov†www.commerce.gov】 【100†Science.gov†www.science.gov】 【101†USA.gov†www.usa.gov】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDLMF: §22.5 Special Values ‣ Properties ‣ Chapter 22 Jacobian Elliptic Functions (https://dlmf.nist.gov/22.5)\nciteturn1243view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://dlmf.nist.gov/22.5\",\"lineno\":30}); Total lines: 155\nL0: 【0†DLMF】\nL1: \nL2:   * 【1†Index】\nL3:   * 【2†Notations】\nL4:   * [Input][Button: Search]\nL5: \nL6:   * 【3†Help?】\nL7:   * 【4†Citing】\nL8:   * 【5†Customize】\nL9:   * AnnotateUnAnnotate\nL10:   * 【6†About the Project】\nL11: \nL12: 【7†22 Jacobian Elliptic Functions】【8†Properties】【9†22.4 Periods, Poles, and Zeros】【10†22.6 Elementary Identities】\nL13: \nL14: # §22.5 Special Values\nL15: \nL16: ⓘ\nL17: \nL18: Keywords:\nL19:     【11†Jacobian elliptic functions】, 【12†special values of the variable】\nL20: Permalink:\nL21:     【13†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.5】\nL22: See also:\nL23:     Annotations for 【14†Ch.22】\nL24: ###### Contents\nL25: \nL26:   1. 【15†§22.5(i) Special Values of $z$】\nL27:   2. 【16†§22.5(ii) Limiting Values of $k$】\nL28: ## §22.5(i) Special Values of $z$\nL29: \nL30: ⓘ\nL31: \nL32: Keywords:\nL33:     【11†Jacobian elliptic functions】, 【12†special values of the variable】\nL34: Notes:\nL35:     See Lawden (【17†1989】, pp. 26–30), Whittaker and Watson (【18†1927】, pp. 498–505).\nL36: Permalink:\nL37:     【19†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.5.i】\nL38: See also:\nL39:     Annotations for 【20†§22.5】 and 【14†Ch.22】\nL40: Table 【21†22.5.1】 gives the value of each of the 12 Jacobian elliptic functions, together with its $z$-derivative (or at a pole, the residue), for values of $z$ that are integer multiples of $K$, $\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$. For example, at $z=K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$, $\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)=1/k$, $d\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)/dz=0$. (The modulus $k$ is suppressed throughout the table.)\nL41: Table 22.5.1: Jacobian elliptic function values, together with derivatives or residues, for special values of the variable.\nL42:  | $z$\nL43: --- | ---\nL44:  | $0$  | $K$  | $K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $2K$  | $2K+2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$  | $2\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$\nL45: --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL46: $\\mathrm{sn}z$  | $0,1$  | $1,0$  | $1/k,0$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty }$, $1/k$  | $0,-1$  | $0,-1$  | $0,1$\nL47: $\\mathrm{cn}z$  | $1,0$  | $0,-{k}^{\\prime }$  | $-\\mathrm{i}{k}^{\\prime }/k,0$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty }$, $-\\mathrm{i}/k$  | $-1,0$  | $1,0$  | $-1,0$\nL48: $\\mathrm{dn}z$  | $1,0$  | ${k}^{\\prime },0$  | $0,\\mathrm{i}{k}^{\\prime }$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty }$, $-\\mathrm{i}$  | $1,0$  | $-1,0$  | $-1,0$\nL49: $\\mathrm{cd}z$  | $1,0$  | $0,-1$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },-{k}^{-1}$  | ${k}^{-1},0$  | $-1,0$  | $-1,0$  | $1,0$\nL50: $\\mathrm{sd}z$  | $0,1$  | $k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1},0$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },-\\mathrm{i}{(k{k}^{\\prime })}^{-1}$  | $\\mathrm{i}{k}^{-1},0$  | $0,-1$  | $0,1$  | $0,-1$\nL51: $\\mathrm{nd}z$  | $1,0$  | $k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1},0$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },-\\mathrm{i}k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1}$  | $0,\\mathrm{i}$  | $1,0$  | $-1,0$  | $-1,0$\nL52: $\\mathrm{dc}z$  | $1,0$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },-1$  | $0,k$  | $k,0$  | $-1,0$  | $-1,0$  | $1,0$\nL53: $\\mathrm{nc}z$  | $1,0$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },-k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1}$  | $\\mathrm{i}kk_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1},0$  | $0,\\mathrm{i}k$  | $-1,0$  | $1,0$  | $-1,0$\nL54: $\\mathrm{sc}z$  | $0,1$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },-k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1}$  | $\\mathrm{i}k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{-1},0$  | $\\mathrm{i},0$  | $0,1$  | $0,-1$  | $0,-1$\nL55: $\\mathrm{ns}z$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },1$  | $1,0$  | $k,0$  | $0,k$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },-1$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },-1$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },1$\nL56: $\\mathrm{ds}z$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },1$  | ${k}^{\\prime },0$  | $0,\\mathrm{i}k{k}^{\\prime }$  | $-\\mathrm{i}k,0$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },-1$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },1$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },-1$\nL57: $\\mathrm{cs}z$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },1$  | $0,-{k}^{\\prime }$  | $-\\mathrm{i}{k}^{\\prime },0$  | $-\\mathrm{i},0$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },1$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },-1$  | $\\mathrm{\\infty },-1$\nL58: ⓘ\nL59: Symbols:\nL60:     【22†$\\mathrm{cd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【23†$\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【24†$\\mathrm{cs}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【22†$\\mathrm{dc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【25†$\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【26†$\\mathrm{ds}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【23†$\\mathrm{nc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【25†$\\mathrm{nd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【27†$\\mathrm{ns}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【24†$\\mathrm{sc}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【26†$\\mathrm{sd}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【27†$\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【28†${K}^{\\prime }\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complementary complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【29†$K\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【30†$\\mathrm{i}$: imaginary unit】, 【31†$z$: complex】, 【32†$k$: modulus】 and 【33†${k}^{\\prime }$: complementary modulus】\nL61: A&S Ref:\nL62:     Table 16.7\nL63: Referenced by:\nL64:     【34†§22.20(ii)】, 【35†§22.5(i)】\nL65: Permalink:\nL66:     【36†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.5.T1】\nL67: See also:\nL68:     Annotations for 【37†§22.5(i)】, 【20†§22.5】 and 【14†Ch.22】\nL69: Table 【38†22.5.2】 gives $\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$, $\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$, $\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$ for other special values of $z$. For example, $\\mathrm{sn}(\\frac{1}{2}K,k)={(1+{k}^{\\prime })}^{-1/2}$. For the other nine functions ratios can be taken; compare (【39†22.2.10】).\nL70: Table 22.5.2: Other special values of Jacobian elliptic functions.\nL71:  | $z$\nL72:  | $\\frac{1}{2}K$  | $\\frac{1}{2}(K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime })$  | $\\frac{1}{2}\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$\nL73: $\\mathrm{sn}z$  | ${(1+{k}^{\\prime })}^{-1/2}$  | $\\left({(1+k)}^{1/2}+\\mathrm{i}{(1-k)}^{1/2}\\right)/{(2k)}^{1/2}$  | $\\mathrm{i}{k}^{-1/2}$\nL74: $\\mathrm{cn}z$  | ${({k}^{\\prime }/(1+{k}^{\\prime }))}^{1/2}$  | $(1-\\mathrm{i})k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{1/2}/{(2k)}^{1/2}$  | ${(1+k)}^{1/2}{k}^{-1/2}$\nL75: $\\mathrm{dn}z$  | $k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{1/2}$  | $\\frac{1-\\mathrm{i}}{2}k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{1/2}\\left({(1+k)}^{1/2}+\\mathrm{i}{(1-k)}^{1/2}\\right)$  | ${(1+k)}^{1/2}$\nL76:  | $z$\nL77:  | $\\frac{3}{2}K$  | $\\frac{3}{2}(K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime })$  | $\\frac{3}{2}\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime }$\nL78: $\\mathrm{sn}z$  | ${(1+{k}^{\\prime })}^{-1/2}$  | $\\left({(1+k)}^{1/2}+\\mathrm{i}{(1-k)}^{1/2}\\right)/{(2k)}^{1/2}$  | $-\\mathrm{i}{k}^{-1/2}$\nL79: $\\mathrm{cn}z$  | $-{({k}^{\\prime }/(1+{k}^{\\prime }))}^{1/2}$  | $(1-\\mathrm{i})k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{1/2}/{(2k)}^{1/2}$  | $-{(1+k)}^{1/2}{k}^{-1/2}$\nL80: $\\mathrm{dn}z$  | $k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{1/2}$  | $\\frac{\\mathrm{i}-1}{2}k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{1/2}\\left({(1+k)}^{1/2}+\\mathrm{i}{(1-k)}^{1/2}\\right)$  | $-{(1+k)}^{1/2}$\nL81: ⓘ\nL82: Symbols:\nL83:     【23†$\\mathrm{cn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【25†$\\mathrm{dn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【27†$\\mathrm{sn}(z,k)$: Jacobian elliptic function】, 【40†$\\pi $: the ratio of the circumference of a circle to its diameter】, 【28†${K}^{\\prime }\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complementary complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【29†$K\\left(k\\right)$: Legendre’s complete elliptic integral of the first kind】, 【30†$\\mathrm{i}$: imaginary unit】, 【41†$\\mathrm{ph}$: phase】, 【31†$z$: complex】, 【32†$k$: modulus】 and 【33†${k}^{\\prime }$: complementary modulus】\nL84: A&S Ref:\nL85:     Table 16.5\nL86: Referenced by:\nL87:     【42†§22.5(i)】, 【43†Erratum (V1.0.7) for Table 22.5.2】, 【44†Erratum (V1.1.10) for Table 22.5.2】\nL88: Permalink:\nL89:     【45†http://dlmf.nist.gov/22.5.T2】\nL90: Correction (effective with 1.1.10):\nL91:     The entry for $\\mathrm{sn}z$, $z=\\frac{3}{2}(K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime })$, which previously was $(1+\\mathrm{i})({(1+{k}^{\\prime })}^{1/2}-\\mathrm{i}{(1-{k}^{\\prime })}^{1/2})/(2{k}^{1/2})$ has been corrected to be $\\left({(1+k)}^{1/2}+\\mathrm{i}{(1-k)}^{1/2}\\right)/{(2k)}^{1/2}$. The previous result was correct only for $|\\mathrm{ph}k|<\\frac{1}{2}\\pi $. Furthermore, the presentation of several of the other results in the middle column have been simplfied.\nL92: Suggested 2023-03-06 by Alan Barnes\nL93: Errata (effective with 1.0.7):\nL94:     The entry for $\\mathrm{sn}z$ at $z=\\frac{3}{2}(K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime })$ has been corrected. The correct entry is $(1+\\mathrm{i})({(1+{k}^{\\prime })}^{1/2}-\\mathrm{i}{(1-{k}^{\\prime })}^{1/2})/(2{k}^{1/2})$. Originally the terms ${(1+{k}^{\\prime })}^{1/2}$ and ${(1-{k}^{\\prime })}^{1/2}$ were given incorrectly as ${(1+k)}^{1/2}$ and ${(1-k)}^{1/2}$. Similarly, the entry for $\\mathrm{dn}z$ at $z=\\frac{3}{2}(K+\\mathrm{i}{K}^{\\prime })$ has been corrected.\nL95: The correct entry is $(-1+\\mathrm{i})k_{}^{\\prime }{}_{}{}^{1/2}({(1+k)}^{1/2}+\\mathrm{i}{(1-k)}^{1/2})/2$. Originally the terms ${(1+k)}^{1/2}$ and ${(1-k)}^{1/2}$ were given incorrectly as ${(1+{k}^{\\prime })}^{1/2}$ and ${(1-{k}^{\\prime })}^{1/2}$.\nL96: Reported 2014-02-28 by Svante Janson\nL97: \nL98: See also:\n"

